---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import site from "../../data/site.json";
import timeline from "../../data/timeline.json";
---

<BaseLayout title={`Portfolio | ${site.siteName}`} description={`${site.siteName}'s career timeline, business systems experience, CRM and ERP transformation work, and applied AI focus.`}>
  <main>
    <section class="page-hero portrait-hero">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Portfolio</p>
        <h1>A working life built around people, process, and systems.</h1>
        <p>I work between business teams and technology delivery, helping organizations make complex operations clearer and more useful.</p>
        <a class="secondary-link timeline-jump" href="#career-timeline">View career timeline</a>
      </div>
      <div class="page-hero-art" aria-label={`${site.siteName} CRM and AI focus`}>
        <img src="/assets/hero-ribbons.png" alt="" aria-hidden="true" />
        <strong>CRM<br />+ AI</strong>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section timeline-section" id="career-timeline">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <div><p class="eyebrow">Career timeline</p><h2>How the work evolved.</h2></div>
        <p class="timeline-note">A concise working timeline — from graduation to CRM, ERP, and applied AI.</p>
      </div>
      <ol class="career-timeline">
        {timeline.entries.map((entry) => (
          <li>
            <div class="timeline-period">{entry.period}</div>
            <div class="timeline-marker" aria-hidden="true"></div>
            <div class="timeline-content">
              <p class="eyebrow">{entry.location}</p>
              <h3>{entry.title}</h3>
              <p>{entry.summary}</p>
              <div class="tag-list">{entry.themes.map((theme) => <span>{theme}</span>)}</div>
            </div>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="section detail-grid">
      <article><span>Current focus</span><h3>Dynamics 365, Copilot, and Power Platform</h3><p>CRM modernization, intelligent service workflows, sales operations, automation, reporting, and adoption.</p></article>
      <article><span>Education</span><h3>Southwest Jiaotong University</h3><p>Founded in 1896, SWJTU is known for engineering and transportation disciplines. That background shaped how I think about systems, process, and scale.</p></article>
      <article><span>Professional setting</span><h3>Canadian business systems work</h3><p>My recent work is centered on CRM, customer operations, and system modernization in Canadian business contexts.</p></article>
      <article><span>Certifications</span><h3>Microsoft business applications path</h3><p>Dynamics 365, Power Platform, Dataverse, Power Automate, Copilot, and solution delivery practices.</p></article>
    </section>

    <section class="section split-section">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">How I work</p><h2>How I usually add value.</h2></div>
      <div class="copy-block">
        <p>I clarify the real workflow behind a request: who owns the data, where handoffs happen, what exceptions matter, and what users need to see when they make decisions.</p>
        <p>Then I turn that into useful delivery artifacts: user stories, acceptance criteria, process maps, CRM behavior, automation rules, test scenarios, and rollout notes.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">Strengths</p><h2>Where I tend to be useful.</h2></div>
      <div class="soft-card-grid">
        <article><h3>Business process discovery</h3><p>Finding the real process behind the system request.</p></article>
        <article><h3>CRM functional design</h3><p>Turning sales, service, and customer records into usable CRM behavior.</p></article>
        <article><h3>Power Platform automation</h3><p>Replacing repetitive manual work with controlled, explainable workflows.</p></article>
        <article><h3>User adoption</h3><p>Helping business users understand why a new system makes daily work easier.</p></article>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
